Underneath a soft week of US data, order books are full and prices are still climbing.

@AndreasSteno explains how these orders held up across manufacturing and services, and most firms report paying more.

His read: slow-ish growth running straight into sticky inflation.

Yields won't fall on numbers this soft while prices stay this firm, which keeps the Fed boxed in.

@AndreasSteno Steno's breaking down the macro during the Live trading workshop in our free Trading League.

